{"title":"KVPY","category":"Engineering","bank":"kvpy","subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Limits","count":12,"questions":[{"id":51709,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Limits","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"Let $g(x)=\\int_{0}^{|x|^{2 / 4}} t^{2 / 3} \\sin \\frac{1}{t} d t$, for all real $x$. Then $\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{\\mathrm{g}(\\mathrm{x})}{\\mathrm{x}}$ is equal to","options":["$\\infty$","$-\\infty$","0","$\\frac{3}{4}$"],"answer":0,"solution":"Apply L hospital rule\n$\\begin{array}{l}\ng^{\\prime}(x)=|x|^{1 / 2} \\sin \\left(\\frac{1}{|x|^{3 / 4}}\\right) \\\\\n\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0} g^{\\prime}(X) \\\\\n\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0}|x|^{1 / 2} \\sin \\left(\\frac{1}{|x|^{3 / 4}}\\right)=0\n\\end{array}$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2017 (19 Nov SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d213a92b6ae766712c41"},{"id":51710,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Limits","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"Let $a\\gt 0$ be a real number. Then the limit $\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 2} \\frac{a^{x}+a^{3-x}-\\left(a^{2}+a\\right)}{a^{3-x}-a^{x / 2}}$\nis","options":["$2 \\log a$","$-\\frac{4}{3} a$","$\\frac{a^{2}+a}{2}$","$\\frac{2}{3}(1-a)$"],"answer":3,"solution":"$\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 2} \\frac{a^{x}+a^{3-x}-\\left(a^{2}+a\\right)}{a^{3-x}-a^{x / 2}}\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 2} \\frac{\\left(a^{x}-a\\right)\\left(a^{x / 2}-a\\right)\\left(a^{x / 2}+a\\right)}{\\left(a-a^{x / 2}\\right)\\left(a^{2}+a^{x}+a^{x / 2} \\cdot a\\right)}\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 2}-\\frac{\\left(a^{x}-a\\right)\\left(a^{x / 2}+a\\right)}{a^{2}+a^{x}+a^{x / 2} \\cdot a}=\\frac{2}{3}(1-a)$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2015 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d213fce87ef488394f1c"},{"id":51711,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Limits","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"Limit $\\lim _{x \\rightarrow \\infty} x^{2} \\int_{0}^{x} e^{t^{3}-x^{3}}$ dt equals","options":["$\\frac{1}{3}$","2","$\\infty$","$\\frac{2}{3}$"],"answer":0,"solution":"\n\\lim _{x \\rightarrow \\infty} \\frac{x^{2} \\int_{0}^{x} e^{x^{3}} d t}{e^{x^{3}}}\n\nApply L Hospital\n\n\\begin{array}{l}\n\\lim _{x \\rightarrow \\infty} \\frac{2 x \\int_{0}^{x} e^{t^{3}}+x^{2} e^{x^{3}}}{3 x^{2} e^{x^{3}}} \\\\\n\\lim _{x \\rightarrow \\infty} \\frac{2 \\int_{0}^{x} e^{t^{3}}+x e^{x^{3}}}{3 x e^{x^{3}}} \\\\\n\\lim _{x \\rightarrow \\infty} \\frac{2 e^{x^{3}}+e^{x^{3}}+3 x^{3} e^{x^{3}}}{3 e^{x^{3}}+9 x^{3} e^{x^{3}}} \\\\\n\\lim _{x \\rightarrow \\infty} \\frac{3+3 x^{3}}{3+9 x^{3}}=\\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{array}\n","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2016 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d21306e672a38d06daeb"},{"id":51712,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Limits","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"<p>Consider the following statements<br />\nI. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>→</mo><mo>∞</mo></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></mfrac></math> does not exist<br />\nII. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>→</mo><mo>∞</mo></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></mfrac></math> does not exist<br />\nThen</p>","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> is true and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> is false","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> is false and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> is true","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> are true","neither Inor <math xmlns=\"http://www.