{x}}\\right)=\\frac{1}{2+2}=\\frac{1}{4}$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2017 (5 Nov SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d213595054ddcbb7e099"},{"id":51714,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Limits","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"The value of $\\lim _{n \\rightarrow \\infty}\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4 n^{2}-1}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4 n^{2}-4}}+\\ldots+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4 n^{2}-n^{2}}}\\right)$ is -","options":["$\\frac{1}{4}$","$\\frac{\\pi}{12}$","$\\frac{\\pi}{4}$","$\\frac{\\pi}{6}$"],"answer":3,"solution":"$\\lim _{n \\rightarrow \\infty} \\sum_{r=1}^{n} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4 n^{2}-r^{2}}}=\\lim _{n \\rightarrow \\infty} \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{r=1}^{n} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-(r / n)^{2}}}=\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{d x}{\\sqrt{4-x^{2}}}=\\left(\\sin ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)\\right)_{0}^{1}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2011 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d213659094d65644b703"},{"id":51715,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Limits","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"Suppose the limit <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>→</mo><mo>∞</mo></mrow></munder><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi>n</mi></msup></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></math> exists and is larger than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math> Then,","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo><</mo><mi>L</mi><mo><</mo><mn>2</mn></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo><</mo><mi>L</mi><mo><</mo><mn>3</mn></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo><</mo><mi>L</mi><mo><</mo><mn>3</mn></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></math>"],"